  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 130 PM MST Wed Nov 4 2026\n\nNo major changes in the long term, except for taking out Friday\nand starting the long term discussion on Saturday, please see\nprevious discussion below...\n\nSaturday...Will see a slow warming trend though tempered by \nnortherly flow aloft. Low and mid levels look too dry for any \nprecipitation.\n\nSunday...The warming trend continues as the ridge aloft builds \nacross our counties, helping to produce a surface lee trough across \neastern Wyoming. 700 mb temperatures near 7 Celsius will yield \nmaximum temperatures from the mid 50s to mid 60s.\n\nMonday-Wednesday...Dry west northwest flow aloft prevails with a few \nshortwave troughs aloft passing by, though with minimal low and mid \nlevel moisture, no precipitation expected. High temperatures nearly \nthe same each day based on 700 mb temperatures.",
